    "source": "sharegpt",
    "why": "SYMMETRIC PAIR. Every co-tenancy tier in this study pairs UNLIKE models, so 'does MPS create systematic winners and losers' has only ever been answered by argument. Two identical Qwen2.5-1.5B-AWQ instances remove the confound: same weights, same quota, same kernels, same trace weight. FINDINGS 8 established that MPS reallocates toward IN-FLIGHT DEPTH rather than model size -- T5's 7B ran 11.11 concurrent against the 1.5B's 2.84 and won; T11's hammered 1.5B ran 8.47 against 1.51 and won. Identical tenants under identical load have identical depth, so the prediction is NEAR-SYMMETRIC degradation on both arms and an aggregate MPS gain at or above T5's, two identical decoders being the most composition-similar pair possible. Also yields the Gini coefficient the external review asked for, comparable to the published 0.35-MPS / 0.12-MIG figures."
  },
